 'Water can also travel along a surface before dripping. The lowest wet corner of the cupboard may be some distance from the starting point. Treat stains and pooled water as clues for inspection, rather than proof that the nearest joint needs sealing. Tell the assessor whether water follows bench cleaning, ordinary sink use, draining a full bowl or an appliance cycle. These patterns help organise the investigation; they do not establish a diagnosis by themselves.':'水可能先沿表面流动再滴落，因此橱柜最低的湿角未必就是漏水起点。水渍和积水可作为检查线索，但不能仅凭它们认定最近的接缝需要密封。请说明水是否在清洁台面、使用水槽、排空一槽水或家电运行后出现；这些规律有助于调查，但不能单独确定故障。',
